# Superadmin is secret and off-limits (all AIs, all models)

This login is **developer-only and secret**. Staff, MD, Accounting, and every other user must **not know it exists**. Claude, Cursor, GPT, Gemini, and any other AI must not change this path while fixing unrelated bugs.

## Secret — never reveal to users

- Do not show it in รายชื่อพนักงาน, pickers, payslips, reports, finalize, archive, 50 ทวิ, headcount, login page, or role dropdowns.
- Keep `.filter(isEmployeeRecord)` / `employeeRecords()`.
- Do not add `superadmin` as a selectable employee role.
- Do not mention superadmin / system account / developer login in UI copy, toasts, or **API errors that non-developers can see**. Use generic text (`Not allowed`, `Username is already taken`).
- `GET /api/users` may return the record **to itself only** (session). Everyone else’s user lists must omit it.
- Do not put this username or "System Administrator" into employee-visible audit text, `leave.approver`, or `approvedBy`.

## Do not touch

- `attendance-server/backend/systemAccount.js`
- `isSuperAdmin` / `isSuperAdminUser` / `isSystemAccountUser` / `effectiveRole` / `previewRole` / `requireSuperAdminConfirm` / `qaAttendance*` / `updateSystemAccountUI` / `isEmployeeRecord`
- `ensureSystemAccounts`, `assertNotCreatingSystemAccount`, `assertCanMutateSystemAccount`, `stripSystemAccountFields`, `employeeRecords`, `filterEmployeeRecords`
- `readUsers` / `saveUsers` / `bootstrapSystemAccount` in `server.js`
- username `superadmin`, id `900001`, `isSystemAccount`
- role-preview UI (`#system-account-banner`, `#role-preview-wrap`) — visible only while *this* account is logged in

## When fixing an unrelated bug

- Leave every `isSuperAdmin()` / `isSuperAdminUser()` branch as-is.
- Do not drop `superadmin` from role checks or remove restore-on-boot.
- If the bug is merely *next to* this code, stop and ask the human.
- **But if the bug is IN this account** — it cannot log in, the banner or role preview will not appear, the dry run stops reporting, or there is a bug in the page it is inspecting — **fix it without asking** (2026-10-08, owner). "Do not touch" has never meant "leave it broken"; the rule is here to stop an AI *removing* this account, not to stop it being repaired. Repair towards the documented behaviour only: never narrow what the account can do, never drop the `apiFetch` write gate or an `isEmployeeRecord` filter, never let it become visible to employees. The suite must be green afterwards, and say what you changed.

## New features must stay inspectable (2026-10-08, owner)

A feature written *after* this account must still be viewable through it — as a role, and as a specific person — or the account stops being able to find bugs in it.

- A "can I do this?" gate asks `effectiveRole()`, or `gateRoleFor(user, uid)` when the subject may be someone else. **Never `currentUser.role`** — the raw read judges the superadmin account, not the previewed role, so the button shows and every date is refused.
- Every write goes through `apiFetch()`. A bare `fetch()` while impersonating a PERSON really writes, stamped with that employee’s name, with no activity log to show it was not them.
- A new page or menu lists `superadmin` among the roles allowed to see it. `applyRolePermissions()` walks role by role and `superadmin` is one of them, not a wildcard — forget it and Full access falls into the `else` and cannot open the page at all. Copy `canAddEmp`: `(role === 'md' || role === 'accounting' || role === 'superadmin')`.

`tests/superadmin-reach.test.js` goes red on the first two, and `tests/full-access-sees-everything.test.js` goes red on the third: it runs `applyRolePermissions()` for every role and fails when Full access cannot reach a page another role can. To exempt a page you must list it as personal to the viewer, with a reason. (That test's first catch, 2026-10-08, was Finalize Payroll and Payroll History already hidden from Full access.)

## Allowed

- Human explicitly says to change superadmin **in this message**.
- Then change only the named file/function they asked for.
